Title: Extra compiler optimization flags, plus SIMD flags tunable by GN args
Origin: Thorium (https://github.com/Alex313031/thorium), ported

Two independent knobs:

  is_full_optimization_build   clang -O3 instead of -O2, O2 ThinLTO with CGO3
                               in the link step, and a set of -mllvm passes.
                               Defaults to is_official_build, as in Thorium, so
                               the release builds assets/args/ describes get it
                               and a debug or developer build does not. The
                               binaries are around 40% larger.
  electron_x86_profile         the ISA baseline target code may assume, "none"
                               through "avx512_skx", each level carrying its
                               own -mtune and -ffp-contract policy. Defaults
                               follow Thorium: sse2 on x86, sse3 on x64, which
                               is also what Chromium itself assumes on x64.

The 32-bit default is about correctness here rather than speed.
patches/chromium/build/0221-require-sse3-on-x86-platforms.patch lowers
Chromium's x86 baseline back to SSE2 for the pre-SSE3 machines these builds
exist to support, so an x86 profile of sse3 or above would quietly undo it.

  build/config/compiler_opt.gni      new. Declares both args, validates the
                                     profile against the target, and expands it
                                     into the cflag/rustflag lists the configs
                                     below consume.
  build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn        declares electron_x86_profile with its
                                     per-arch default -- it has to be set here
                                     rather than in compiler_opt.gni because
                                     toolchain files override it in
                                     toolchain_args, which cannot reference a
                                     .gni the toolchain does not import --
                                     appends :electron_x86_isa to
                                     default_compiler_configs, and redirects
                                     host_toolchain for the AVX-512 case below.
  build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn     the configs. :electron_x86_isa holds the
                                     ISA flags and applies to all target code;
                                     :electron_x86_tune and :electron_arm_tune
                                     hold tuning and hang off
                                     :compiler_codegen, which is where
                                     Chromium keeps flags that only affect code
                                     generation. Plus the -ffp-contract hook in
                                     :compiler, the two thinlto_optimize_* link
                                     policies, and -O3 in :optimize and
                                     :optimize_max.
  build/toolchain/linux/BUILD.gn     clang_x64_electron_build_host.
  build/toolchain/gcc_toolchain.gni  pins the Rust host build tools toolchain
                                     to profile "none"; it builds code that
                                     runs during the build.
  electron/BUILD.gn                  electron_lib on optimize_max.

Host ISA. Anything executed during the build -- mksnapshot, protoc, the
snapshot generator -- runs on the build machine, so it must not be handed
features that machine lacks. A cross build gets this for free: those tools are
compiled in the Linux host toolchain, whose current_os does not match
target_os, so is_a_target_toolchain is false and no profile flags reach them.
In a native build host_toolchain is the default toolchain and that distinction
disappears, which is why avx512_skx on Linux x64 routes host_toolchain to a
separate baseline toolchain. Below AVX-512 a native build does compile
build-time tools with the profile's flags, on the assumption that a machine
asked to target itself can run the result. A native Windows build has no
equivalent redirect, so avx512_skx there needs an AVX-512 builder.

Not carried over from Thorium's version of this change:

  is_thorium_build             a brand flag, with nothing to gate here.
  thorium_* identifiers        renamed electron_*.
  -w and -Awarnings            Thorium silences every compiler and rustc
                               warning. Not a decision to inherit silently.
  copyright header rewrites    Thorium restamps the files it touches.
  /OPT:LLDTAILMERGE, /PROFILE  linker flags unrelated to either knob.
  required_cpu_features, and the installer and package name labels
                               Thorium's own packaging.
  the -msse3 removals in build/config/compiler_cpu_abi.gn and
  build/config/win/BUILD.gn    the same x86 baseline change patch 0221 above
                               already makes, differently.

Two things this does that Thorium did not:

  config("optimize")   Thorium raised :optimize_max to -O3 and left :optimize
                       alone, but default_optimization resolves to :optimize,
                       so nearly the whole tree kept clang-cl's explicit
                       /clang:-O2 -- the one flag the knob exists to drop.
                       is_full_optimization_build now reaches there too. This
                       was a bug on Thorium's side, fixed there as well.
  electron_lib         swaps default_optimization for optimize_max, so
                       Electron's own C++ is compiled for speed rather than
                       inheriting whatever the rest of the tree gets.

diff --git a/build/config/compiler_opt.gni b/build/config/compiler_opt.gni
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5cb4433
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/config/compiler_opt.gni
@@ -0,0 +1,183 @@
+# Copyright (c) 2026 Alex313031
+# Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
+# found in the LICENSE file.
+#
+# Aggressive optimization and x86 SIMD tuning, ported from Thorium.
+#
+# is_full_optimization_build follows is_official_build, as it does in Thorium,
+# so the release builds this repo exists to produce get it and a local debug or
+# developer build does not.
+#
+# electron_x86_profile does apply by default, following Thorium: sse2 for x86
+# and sse3 for x64 (set in //build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn). The 32-bit default
+# matters -- the win7 series lowers Chromium's x86 baseline back from SSE3 in
+# patches/chromium/build/0221-require-sse3-on-x86-platforms.patch, so raising
+# it here would undo that for the machines this build exists to support.
+#
+# The x64 default stays at Chromium's SSE3, since the only x64 CPUs without it
+# are pre-Venice K8s.
+
+import("//build/config/compiler/compiler.gni")
+import("//build/toolchain/toolchain.gni")
+
+declare_args() {
+  # Raise optimization above what Chromium ships: -O3 instead of -O2, O2
+  # ThinLTO with CGO3 in the link step, and a handful of LLVM passes. Faster
+  # and substantially larger. Set it to false for a release build that should
+  # match what upstream Electron would produce.
+  is_full_optimization_build = is_official_build
+
+  # Tune for the Raspberry Pi on Linux ARM64.
+  is_raspi = false
+}
+
+_x86_profile_platform =
+    is_win || is_linux || is_mac || is_android || is_chromeos || is_fuchsia
+
+_x86_profile_is_valid =
+    electron_x86_profile == "none" || electron_x86_profile == "sse2" ||
+    electron_x86_profile == "sse3" || electron_x86_profile == "sse4_1" ||
+    electron_x86_profile == "sse4_2" || electron_x86_profile == "avx" ||
+    electron_x86_profile == "avx_fma" || electron_x86_profile == "avx2" ||
+    electron_x86_profile == "avx2_fma" || electron_x86_profile == "avx512_skx"
+assert(_x86_profile_is_valid,
+       "Unsupported electron_x86_profile: " + electron_x86_profile)
+assert(electron_x86_profile == "none" || _x86_profile_platform,
+       "electron_x86_profile is not supported for this target platform")
+assert(electron_x86_profile == "none" || target_cpu == "x86" ||
+           target_cpu == "x64",
+       "electron_x86_profile requires an x86 or x64 target")
+
+if (is_debug) {
+  assert(!is_full_optimization_build,
+         "is_full_optimization_build only works with non-debug builds")
+}
+
+electron_x86_isa_cflags = []
+electron_x86_isa_rustflags = []
+electron_x86_tune_cflags = []
+electron_x86_tune_rustflags = []
+electron_x86_numeric_cflags = []
+electron_x86_numeric_rustflags = []
+
+_apply_x86_profile =
+    is_a_target_toolchain && !toolchain_for_rust_host_build_tools &&
+    _x86_profile_platform && (current_cpu == "x86" || current_cpu == "x64")
+
+# A ChromeOS device toolchain with an explicit -march owns its complete ISA.
+if (defined(cros_target_cpu_arch) && cros_target_cpu_arch != "") {
+  _apply_x86_profile = false
+}
+
+if (_apply_x86_profile) {
+  if (electron_x86_profile == "sse2") {
+    electron_x86_isa_cflags = [ "-msse2" ]
+    electron_x86_isa_rustflags = [ "-Ctarget-feature=+sse2" ]
+  } else if (electron_x86_profile == "sse3") {
+    electron_x86_isa_cflags = [ "-msse3" ]
+    electron_x86_isa_rustflags = [ "-Ctarget-feature=+sse3" ]
+  } else if (electron_x86_profile == "sse4_1") {
+    electron_x86_isa_cflags = [
+      "-msse3",
+      "-mssse3",
+      "-msse4.1",
+    ]
+    electron_x86_isa_rustflags = [ "-Ctarget-feature=+sse3,+ssse3,+sse4.1" ]
+    electron_x86_tune_cflags = [ "-mtune=core2" ]
+    electron_x86_tune_rustflags = [ "-Ztune-cpu=core2" ]
+  } else if (electron_x86_profile == "sse4_2") {
+    electron_x86_isa_cflags = [
+      "-msse3",
+      "-mssse3",
+      "-msse4.1",
+      "-msse4.2",
+    ]
+    electron_x86_isa_rustflags =
+        [ "-Ctarget-feature=+sse3,+ssse3,+sse4.1,+sse4.2" ]
+    electron_x86_tune_cflags = [ "-mtune=nehalem" ]
+    electron_x86_tune_rustflags = [ "-Ztune-cpu=nehalem" ]
+  } else if (electron_x86_profile == "avx") {
+    electron_x86_isa_cflags = [
+      "-msse3",
+      "-mavx",
+    ]
+    electron_x86_isa_rustflags = [ "-Ctarget-feature=+sse3,+avx,-fast-gather,+prefer-no-gather,+prefer-no-scatter" ]
+    electron_x86_tune_cflags = [
+      "-mtune=sandybridge",
+      "-mno-gather",
+      "-mno-scatter",
+    ]
+    electron_x86_tune_rustflags = [ "-Ztune-cpu=sandybridge" ]
+  } else if (electron_x86_profile == "avx_fma") {
+    electron_x86_isa_cflags = [
+      "-msse3",
+      "-mavx",
+      "-mfma",
+    ]
+    electron_x86_isa_rustflags = [ "-Ctarget-feature=+sse3,+avx,+fma,-fast-gather,+prefer-no-gather,+prefer-no-scatter" ]
+    electron_x86_tune_cflags = [
+      "-mtune=piledriver",
+      "-mno-gather",
+      "-mno-scatter",
+    ]
+    electron_x86_tune_rustflags = [ "-Ztune-cpu=bdver2" ]
+  } else if (electron_x86_profile == "avx2" ||
+             electron_x86_profile == "avx2_fma" ||
+             electron_x86_profile == "avx512_skx") {
+    electron_x86_isa_cflags = [
+      "-msse3",
+      "-mavx",
+      "-mavx2",
+    ]
+    _rust_target_features = "+sse3,+avx,+avx2"
+
+    if (electron_x86_profile == "avx2_fma" ||
+        electron_x86_profile == "avx512_skx") {
+      electron_x86_isa_cflags += [
+        "-mfma",
+        "-mf16c",
+      ]
+      _rust_target_features += ",+fma,+f16c"
+    }
+
+    if (electron_x86_profile == "avx512_skx") {
+      electron_x86_isa_cflags += [
+        "-mavx512f",
+        "-mavx512cd",
+        "-mavx512vl",
+        "-mavx512bw",
+        "-mavx512dq",
+      ]
+      _rust_target_features +=
+          ",+avx512f,+avx512cd,+avx512vl,+avx512bw,+avx512dq"
+      electron_x86_tune_cflags = [ "-mtune=skylake-avx512" ]
+      electron_x86_tune_rustflags = [ "-Ztune-cpu=skylake-avx512" ]
+    } else {
+      electron_x86_tune_cflags = [ "-mtune=skylake" ]
+      electron_x86_tune_rustflags = [ "-Ztune-cpu=skylake" ]
+    }
+
+    _rust_target_features +=
+        ",-fast-gather,+prefer-no-gather,+prefer-no-scatter"
+    electron_x86_isa_rustflags = [ "-Ctarget-feature=" + _rust_target_features ]
+    electron_x86_tune_cflags += [
+      "-mno-gather",
+      "-mno-scatter",
+    ]
+  }
+
+  # Contraction of a*b+c into an FMA changes results, so it is only allowed
+  # where the profile already requires an FMA-capable CPU.
+  _fp_contract = "off"
+  if (electron_x86_profile == "avx2_fma" ||
+      electron_x86_profile == "avx512_skx") {
+    _fp_contract = "fast"
+  }
+  if (is_win) {
+    electron_x86_numeric_cflags = [ "/clang:-ffp-contract=" + _fp_contract ]
+  } else {
+    electron_x86_numeric_cflags = [ "-ffp-contract=" + _fp_contract ]
+  }
+  electron_x86_numeric_rustflags =
+      [ "-Cllvm-args=-fp-contract=" + _fp_contract ]
+}
diff --git a/build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn b/build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn
index d26beee..0046d0d 100644
--- a/build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn
+++ b/build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn
@@ -175,6 +175,27 @@
                        current_os != "ios" && current_os != "watchos"
 }
 
+# Default x86 feature set, following Thorium: SSE2 on 32-bit, where the win7
+# series deliberately lowered Chromium's baseline back from SSE3, and SSE3 on
+# 64-bit, which practically every x64 CPU has -- only pre-Venice K8 Athlon 64
+# does not.
+_default_electron_x86_profile = "none"
+if (target_os == "win" || target_os == "linux" || target_os == "mac" ||
+    target_os == "android" || target_os == "chromeos" ||
+    target_os == "fuchsia") {
+  if (target_cpu == "x86") {
+    _default_electron_x86_profile = "sse2"
+  } else if (target_cpu == "x64") {
+    _default_electron_x86_profile = "sse3"
+  }
+}
+
+declare_args() {
+  # Minimum x86 CPU feature set for target code. See
+  # //build/config/compiler_opt.gni for the accepted values.
+  electron_x86_profile = _default_electron_x86_profile
+}
+
 assert(!(is_debug && is_official_build), "Can't do official debug builds")
 assert(!(current_os == "ios" && is_component_build),
        "Can't use component build on iOS")
@@ -225,7 +246,14 @@
   # no toolchain omitted host_toolchain from its toolchain_args().
 
   if (host_os == "linux") {
-    if (target_os != "linux") {
+    if (target_os == "linux" && host_cpu == "x64" && target_cpu == "x64" &&
+        electron_x86_profile == "avx512_skx") {
+      # An AVX-512 target can be built on a host that does not implement
+      # AVX-512. Everything executed during the build -- mksnapshot, the V8
+      # snapshot generator, protoc and friends -- has to stay on a baseline
+      # host toolchain or it will fault on this machine.
+      host_toolchain = "//build/toolchain/linux:clang_x64_electron_build_host"
+    } else if (target_os != "linux") {
       host_toolchain = "//build/toolchain/linux:clang_$host_cpu"
     } else if (is_clang) {
       host_toolchain = "//build/toolchain/linux:clang_$host_cpu"
@@ -443,6 +471,10 @@
   default_compiler_configs += [ "//build/config/zos:compiler" ]
 }
 
+# Last, so the ISA requirement cannot be dropped by an earlier config. Empty
+# unless electron_x86_profile is set.
+default_compiler_configs += [ "//build/config/compiler:electron_x86_isa" ]
+
 # Static libraries and source sets use only the compiler ones.
 set_defaults("static_library") {
   configs = default_compiler_configs
